.TH IMPROV-POLICY 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-policy \- Manage a model\*(Aqs access policies (Cedar)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov policy\fR <COMMAND>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage a model\*(Aqs access policies (Cedar).
.PP
A model with no policies is unrestricted. With policies, a user may do only what a policy permits, and a forbid wins. Policies name measures, items, categories and views by id. See improv\-policy\-* and the guide\*(Aqs Access Policies chapter.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
improv\-policy\-validate(1)
Check a policy file against the schema and the model, storing nothing
.TP
improv\-policy\-set(1)
Validate a policy file and store it with the model
.TP
improv\-policy\-show(1)
Print the stored policies, or say there are none
.TP
improv\-policy\-clear(1)
Remove the stored policies: the model is unrestricted again
.TP
improv\-policy\-check(1)
Ask whether a user may do an action, and say which policies decided
.TP
improv\-policy\-template(1)
Print a template\*(Aqs policies, to edit or set
.TP
improv\-policy\-lint(1)
List what a user can infer of what is hidden from them
.SH SEE ALSO
